# 1 Kings Chapter 4 — The EMET Bible (Literal)
**Translator:** EMET | **Source:** Leningrad Codex (B19A)

---

**1** And-the-king Solomon was king over all Israel.

**2** And-these were the-officials who were-his: Azariah son-of Zadok — the-priest;

**3** Elihoreph and-Ahijah, sons-of Shisha — scribes; Jehoshaphat son-of Ahilud — the-recorder;

**4** And-Benaiah son-of Jehoiada — over the-army; and-Zadok and-Abiathar — priests;

**5** And-Azariah son-of Nathan — over the-governors; and-Zabud son-of Nathan — priest, friend-of the-king;

**6** And-Ahishar — over the-house; and-Adoniram son-of Abda — over the-forced-labor.

**7** And-Solomon had twelve governors over all Israel, and-they-provided for the-king and-his-household — each-one a-month in-the-year he-would-provide.

**8** And-these are their-names: Ben-Hur, in-the-hill-country-of Ephraim;

**9** Ben-Deker, in-Makaz and-in-Shaalbim and-Beth-shemesh and-Elon-beth-hanan;

**10** Ben-Hesed, in-Arubboth — to-him was Socoh and-all the-land-of Hepher;

**11** Ben-Abinadab — all the-height-of Dor; Taphath daughter-of Solomon was his-wife;

**12** Baana son-of Ahilud — Taanach and-Megiddo and-all Beth-shan that is beside Zarethan below Jezreel, from-Beth-shan to-Abel-meholah, to beyond Jokmeam;

**13** Ben-Geber, in-Ramoth-gilead — to-him were the-villages-of Jair son-of Manasseh that are in-Gilead; to-him was the-region-of Argob that is in-Bashan, sixty great cities with-walls and-bronze bars;

**14** Ahinadab son-of Iddo — Mahanaim;

**15** Ahimaaz — in-Naphtali; he also took Basemath daughter-of Solomon as-wife;

**16** Baana son-of Hushai — in-Asher and-in-Bealoth;

**17** Jehoshaphat son-of Paruah — in-Issachar;

**18** Shimei son-of Ela — in-Benjamin;

**19** Geber son-of Uri — in-the-land-of Gilead, the-land-of Sihon king-of the-Amorites and-Og king-of Bashan; and-one governor who was in-the-land.

**20** Judah and-Israel were many, as-the-sand that is by the-sea in-multitude, eating and-drinking and-rejoicing.

**21** And-Solomon was ruling over-all the-kingdoms from the-River to-the-land-of the-Philistines and-to the-border-of Egypt. They-were-bringing tribute and-serving Solomon all the-days-of his-life.

**22** And-the-provision-of Solomon for-one day was thirty cors-of fine-flour and-sixty cors-of meal,

**23** ten fattened cattle and-twenty pasture cattle and-a-hundred sheep, besides deer and-gazelles and-roebucks and-fattened fowl.

**24** For he was-ruling over-all the-region across the-River, from-Tiphsah to-Gaza, over-all the-kings across the-River. And-peace was-his on-every side all-around.

**25** And-Judah and-Israel dwelt in-safety, each-man under his-vine and-under his-fig-tree, from-Dan to-Beer-sheba, all the-days-of Solomon.

**26** And-Solomon had forty thousand stalls-of horses for-his-chariots and-twelve thousand horsemen.

**27** And-these governors provided for the-king Solomon and-for-all who-came-near to the-table-of the-king Solomon, each-one in-his-month; they-let-nothing be-lacking.

**28** And-the-barley and-the-straw for-the-horses and-for-the-swift-steeds they-would-bring to the-place where it-would-be, each-one according-to his-charge.

**29** And-God gave wisdom to-Solomon and-understanding exceedingly much, and-breadth-of heart as-the-sand that is on the-shore-of the-sea.

**30** And-the-wisdom-of Solomon was-greater than the-wisdom-of all the-sons-of the-east and-than-all the-wisdom-of Egypt.

**31** And-he-was-wiser than-all men — than-Ethan the-Ezrahite, and-Heman and-Calcol and-Darda, the-sons-of Mahol. And-his-name was in-all the-nations all-around.

**32** And-he-spoke three thousand proverbs, and-his-songs were a-thousand and-five.

**33** And-he-spoke of the-trees, from the-cedar that is in-Lebanon to the-hyssop that-comes-out in-the-wall. And-he-spoke of the-beasts and-of the-birds and-of the-creeping-things and-of the-fish.

**34** And-they-came from-all the-peoples to-hear ʾet-the-wisdom-of Solomon, from-all the-kings-of the-earth who had-heard ʾet-his-wisdom.

---
## EMET Textual Notes

1. **4:6 — "over the-forced-labor" (עַל־הַמַּס)**: The word mas (forced labor/corvée) will become one of the most politically explosive terms in 1 Kings — it is the issue that tears the kingdom apart in chapter 12.

2. **4:20 — "as-the-sand that is by the-sea"**: An echo of the Abrahamic promise (Gen 22:17). Under Solomon, the covenant promise of innumerable descendants appears fulfilled.

3. **4:25 — "under his-vine and-under his-fig-tree"**: This phrase becomes the biblical shorthand for peace and prosperity. Its later use in Micah 4:4 makes it an eschatological hope.

4. **4:29 — "breadth-of heart" (רֹחַב לֵב)**: Not just intelligence but expansiveness of mind — a capacious understanding that encompasses all domains of knowledge.

5. **4:32-33 — the encyclopedic Solomon**: Three thousand proverbs, 1,005 songs, botanical and zoological knowledge. Solomon is presented as the Israelite polymath — wisdom applied across every field.

— EMET
